\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Two lines with different actions}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Let a group of order two act on a pair of complex lines by
fixing the first line pointwise and negating the second at its
nonidentity element. Give the two lines opposite signs of a
[grading](fdip-013N). Swapping coordinates reverses the grading.
A fixed vector would then become a vector on which the same group
element acts by minus one. What could a map that also respects
the group action do to this vector?}
